  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urgent support and protection for at-risk older women and men in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased access to inclusive, protection-based humanitarian support that contributes to their improved security, dignity, and wellbeing for at-risk older women and men with and without disabilities in Ukraine</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will benefit over 5,695 older women and men with and without disabilities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program will specifically address the identified needs and risks faced by older people, including older women and those with disabilities, by providing psychological support to older people affected by the conflict through a case management approach of Home-Based Care (HBC) (whether at home or displaced), Community Safe Space (CSS) activities in locations where IDPs are residing, the provision of personalised assistance as well as targeted conditional cash assistance. We will also ensure the findings of a gender analysis and gender equality are considered throughout the planned programme.</narrative>
  </description>
